usage: flair quantify [-h] --manifest MANIFEST -g GENOME --isoform_bed
                      ISOFORM_BED [-o OUTPUT] [-t THREADS] [--tpm]
                      [--trust_ends] [--generate_map] [--with_gene]
                      [--normalize_ends] [--temp_dir TEMP_DIR]
                      [--keep_intermediate]

Quantify the expression level of isoforms across samples

options:
  -h, --help            show this help message and exit
  -o OUTPUT, --output OUTPUT
                        output file name base for FLAIR quantify (default:
                        flair.quantify)
  -t THREADS, --threads THREADS
                        number of threads: batches of genes counted at once,
                        with minimap2 given any left idle (default: 4)
  --tpm                 also write the counts as transcripts per million,
                        <output>.tpm.tsv
  --trust_ends          count a read for a spliced isoform only if its ends
                        are within 50 bp of the isoform's, for reads of full-
                        length molecules, as from a protocol with little
                        fragmentation
  --generate_map        write each sample's reads by isoform, <output>.<sample
                        id>.read.map.txt: a line of an isoform and its reads,
                        comma-separated
  --with_gene           name each counts row <isoform>_<gene id> rather than
                        <isoform>, its isoform's name and gene id (column 13
                        of the isoform bed)
  --normalize_ends      give each spliced isoform, for counting, the furthest
                        ends of its gene's isoforms with terminal exons like
                        its own, so reads are counted whatever their ends;
                        recommended without --trust_ends when the isoforms of
                        a gene differ only in their ends
  --temp_dir TEMP_DIR   directory for temporary files; each run makes its own
                        directory, named for the output, in it, with the reads
                        and isoforms of each batch of genes realigned
                        (default: $TMPDIR or the system temporary directory)
  --keep_intermediate   keep intermediate and temporary files for debugging,
                        in the run's directory in --temp_dir, which must be
                        given

required named arguments:
  --manifest MANIFEST   tab-separated file of the samples, a line each of four
                        fields: sample id, condition, batch, and the sample's
                        reads aligned to the genome as a sorted, indexed BAM.
                        Blank lines and lines starting with '#' are skipped;
                        each sample id once
  -g GENOME, --genome GENOME
                        FASTA of the genome the reads are aligned to, indexed
                        with samtools faidx (a .fai is made beside it if
                        missing and the directory is writable)
  --isoform_bed ISOFORM_BED
                        the isoforms to count, a FLAIR isoform bed (the 25
                        columns of flair transcriptome, flair combine and
                        flair fusion), whose fusion isoforms are counted too
